---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import GuideSchema from "../../components/GuideSchema.astro";
import GuideNext from "../../components/GuideNext.astro";
import benchmarkData from "../../../data/coefficients.json";
import { calculateBudget } from "../../lib/calculator.js";

const money = value => new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: "USD", maximumFractionDigits: 0 }).format(value);
const bands = benchmarkData.benchmarks.uhaul_one_way_average_by_distance;
const bandRows = bands.map((band, index) => {
  const start = index === 0 ? 1 : bands[index - 1].max_miles + 1;
  const label = band.max_miles === null
    ? `${start.toLocaleString("en-US")} miles or more`
    : `${start.toLocaleString("en-US")} to ${band.max_miles.toLocaleString("en-US")} miles`;
  return { label, average: band.average_usd };
});
// One example distance inside each published band, priced with the calculator's own model.
const exampleDistances = [150, 400, 800, 1250, 1750, 2250, 2800];
const typeColumns = [
  { label: "DIY", type: 0.65 },
  { label: "Rental truck + labor", type: 1 },
  { label: "Full-service movers", type: 1.65 }
];
const exampleRows = exampleDistances.map(distance => ({
  distance,
  totals: typeColumns.map(column => calculateBudget({ distance, size: 1.35, type: column.type }).total)
}));

const title = "What Affects Moving Costs? — Relocation Cost";
const description = "Distance, home size, who does the work, timing and access all change what a move costs. Learn each factor so you can judge any moving estimate.";
const path = "/guides/moving-cost/";
---
<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <GuideSchema title={title} description={description} path={path} />
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-600">Guide</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">How much does moving cost?</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">There is no single price for a move. The cost depends on how far you go, how much you move, who does the work, and a handful of details that are easy to overlook until a quote arrives. This guide explains each factor so you can judge any estimate, including the one from our calculator.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Distance</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">Distance affects fuel, driving time and, for rental trucks, the price itself. One-way truck rentals are priced per route: U-Haul states that its one-way rates depend on the origin, destination, truck size, move date and available inventory. That is why the same mileage can cost different amounts on different routes, and why a distance figure alone can never give you a quote.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Home size and volume</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">More belongings mean a bigger truck or more space on a truck, more labor hours and more packing material. Room count is only a rough proxy. A two-room home full of heavy furniture can need more space than a larger home with little in it. Before you ask for quotes, list the large items, estimate how many boxes you will pack and note anything fragile.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Who does the work</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-slate-700">
      <li><strong>DIY:</strong> you pay for the truck, fuel and equipment, but not for labor. You give your own time and effort.</li>
      <li><strong>Rental truck with hired labor:</strong> you drive, and you pay helpers to load and unload.</li>
      <li><strong>Full-service movers:</strong> movers handle packing, loading, transport and unloading. This has the highest service cost and asks the least of you.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">Our <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/guides/diy-vs-movers/">DIY vs movers guide</a> compares these options in more detail.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Timing and availability</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">Rental availability and mover schedules change with the day of the week, the time of the month and the season. If your dates are flexible, compare quotes for more than one date. A small change in timing can change both the price and whether a truck is available at all.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Access and special items</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">Stairs, long carries from the door to the truck, elevators, parking restrictions, and special items such as pianos, safes or large appliances can add time or require extra handling. Mention them when you request quotes, so the price you are given is closer to the price you pay.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Costs around the move</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">The move itself is only part of the budget. Travel to the new city, temporary housing, deposits, utility setup and packing supplies can add up quickly. Our guide to <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/guides/relocation-budget/">building a relocation budget</a> shows how to keep them in view.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">How the calculator treats these factors</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">The <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/calculator/">moving cost calculator</a> turns distance, home size and move type into a planning estimate. The DIY base is never set below the published U-Haul average for that distance band. The other move types add a labor and service premium, which is a stated assumption and not a market price. Extra costs are added exactly as you enter them, and a 10% buffer is applied on top. The full formula and its limits are on the <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/methodology/">methodology page</a>.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Average one-way truck rental by distance</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">U-Haul publishes average one-way rental prices by distance band ({benchmarkData.sources.uhaul.data_period} data). These are averages across many routes, not quotes for yours, and the average steps up when a move crosses a band boundary.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[20rem] text-left text-sm">
        <caption class="sr-only">U-Haul average one-way truck rental price by distance band</caption>
        <thead class="bg-slate-50 text-slate-600"><tr><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Distance band</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Published average</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
          {bandRows.map(row => (<tr><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-slate-900">{row.label}</th><td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">{money(row.average)}</td></tr>))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Source: <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href={benchmarkData.sources.uhaul.url} rel="noopener">{benchmarkData.sources.uhaul.name}</a>. Prices vary by origin, destination, truck size, move date and inventory.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Planning totals by distance</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">The table below runs one example distance from each band through this site's calculator for a 2–3 room home, with no extra costs entered. The totals include the 10% planning buffer. They show how the three ways of moving compare as distance grows. They are planning estimates, not quotes.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[28rem] text-left text-sm">
        <caption class="sr-only">Planning totals for a 2 to 3 room home by example distance and move type</caption>
        <thead class="bg-slate-50 text-slate-600">
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Example distance</th>
            {typeColumns.map(column => (<th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">{column.label}</th>))}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
          {exampleRows.map(row => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-medium text-slate-900">{row.distance.toLocaleString("en-US")} miles</th>
              {row.totals.map(total => (<td class="px-4 py-3 text-slate-700">{money(total)}</td>))}
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Want your own numbers? Use the <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/calculator/">calculator</a> with your states, home size and extra costs.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Use the estimate to plan, then confirm with quotes</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">Treat any online estimate as a starting point. Ask at least two providers for written estimates based on your actual addresses, dates and inventory, and compare what each one includes.</p>
    <GuideNext current={path} />
  </article>
</Layout>
